You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S02
Scenario title: Equipment-Specific Measurement Workflow
Initial workflow description:
A wafer is measured using one of several tools. The exact preparation and measurement steps differ by tool, and the engineer records the result after measurement.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What criteria or rules determine which measurement tool is selected for a given wafer — for example, wafer type, lot specification, or tool availability?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Can you describe the preparation steps that must be completed before measurement begins, and do these steps differ significantly between tools?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "When the engineer records the measurement result, what exactly does that involve — is it a manual entry into a form or system, a physical log, or does the tool output data automatically?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Do the measurement tools have any data export capability, such as file outputs, network interfaces, or APIs that could be used to retrieve results programmatically?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What happens when a measurement result falls outside the acceptable specification range — is there a defined escalation or rework path?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Approximately how many wafers go through this measurement workflow per shift or per day, and how often does the active tool change during that period?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Measure a wafer using the appropriate equipment-specific procedure and record the result.",
  "actors": [
    "measurement engineer",
    "equipment owner",
    "requester"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "measurement equipment",
    "equipment reservation system",
    "measurement result repository"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "measurement request",
    "wafer identifier",
    "measurement recipe",
    "equipment availability"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "measurement result",
    "equipment usage record",
    "request completion notice"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Confirm measurement request and wafer identifier",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Select suitable measurement equipment",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check equipment availability and reserve slot",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Prepare wafer according to equipment procedure",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Run measurement recipe",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Validate measurement output",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Upload result and notify requester",
      "actor": "measurement engineer"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Which equipment is required for the requested measurement?",
      "branches": [
        "equipment type A",
        "equipment type B",
        "equipment type C"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Is the equipment available and qualified?",
      "branches": [
        "available",
        "unavailable or under maintenance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "condition": "Is the measurement output valid?",
      "branches": [
        "valid",
        "invalid or noisy"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "equipment unavailable",
    "wafer information mismatch",
    "recipe not approved",
    "invalid measurement output"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
